[00:10.06]What are you doing, Lori?
[00:12.42]I’m looking for my T-shirt.
[00:15.30]Your T-shirt?
[00:16.78]You’ve got lots!
[00:18.50]Which one are you looking for?
[00:20.42]The red one with the flower on it.
[00:23.20]I can’t find it anywhere and I’ve got to go out in five minutes.
[00:28.24]Where are you going?
[00:29.42]To the cinema with Lucy and Darcy.
[00:32.54]I want to look nice.
[00:34.26]Oh, I can’t find it!
[00:37.36]Do you want to borrow one of mine?
[00:40.12]Can I?
[00:41.88]Thanks, Olivia, you’re the best.
[00:44.58]Sure.
[00:45.46]Just get one from my room but don’t make a mess.
[00:48.30]Don’t worry.
[00:49.58]No mess, I promise.
[00:52.70]Can I borrow your red boots, too?
[00:55.44]You mean my new ones?
[00:57.18]No, you can’t.
[00:59.72]Oh no, really?
[01:01.28]Why not?
[01:02.48]They’re really cool!
[01:03.88]I know I am the world’s best sister, Lori, but there are some times when I have to say ‘no’!
[01:15.92]Mum?
[01:16.96]Have we got any plans this weekend?
[01:20.06]I don’t think so.
[01:21.92]Why?
[01:22.64]There’s a party at Nathan’s place.
[01:25.14]Can I go?
[01:25.76]Well, that depends …
[01:28.50]When is it?
[01:29.38]Saturday night.
[01:30.52]8 o’clock.
[01:31.86]Sure.
[01:32.64]That’s fine.
[01:33.86]Where does Nathan live?
[01:35.66]He’s out in Foxton.
[01:37.36]His family have got an amazing house.
[01:40.30]Foxton?
[01:41.68]That’s five kilometres from here.
[01:44.78]And I guess there are no buses at that time of night.
[01:49.34]Umm, no, I don’t think so.
[01:52.76]Well, no actually, there aren’t any buses, no.
[01:56.52]Right.
[01:57.70]So come on.
[01:59.35]Let’s hear the next question, Tom.
[02:02.00]Any chance of a lift, Mum?
[02:03.66]Of course, but I need to pick you up by midnight at the latest.
[02:08.50]I need my sleep, you know.
[02:10.58]No problem, Mum.
[02:11.84]Thanks so much!
